request:
a put, then immediately a range on a different member

m1 POST /v3/kv/put  write through m1
    {"key":"bGlu","value":"ZnJlc2g="}
m2 POST /v3/kv/range  read on m2, the very next request
    {"key":"bGlu"}

response:
the value the put wrote, on the first read, with no retry

m1 200 OK
    {"header":{"cluster_id":"12905999167978280553","member_id":"16167093959620304435","revision":"2","raft_term":"2"}}
m2 200 OK
    {"header":{"cluster_id":"12905999167978280553","member_id":"7712592272570853678","revision":"2","raft_term":"2"},"kvs":[{"key":"bGlu","create_revision":"2","mod_revision":"2","version":"1","value":"ZnJlc2g="}],"count":"1"}

request:
the same read, with serializable: true

m1 POST /v3/kv/put  write through m1
    {"key":"bGluLW9wdA==","value":"dg=="}
m3 POST /v3/kv/range  read on m3 without confirming with a quorum
    {"key":"bGluLW9wdA==","serializable":true}

response:
either the new value or nothing at all — both are correct

m1 200 OK
    {"header":{"cluster_id":"12905999167978280553","member_id":"16167093959620304435","revision":"3","raft_term":"2"}}
m3 200 OK
    {"header":{"cluster_id":"12905999167978280553","member_id":"1833274606077085064","revision":"3","raft_term":"2"},"kvs":[{"key":"bGluLW9wdA==","create_revision":"3","mod_revision":"3","version":"1","value":"dg=="}],"count":"1"}
